- op: discuss  # c0d5
  at: '2026-08-09T03:17:40Z'  # c0d5
  by: agent  # c0d5
  actor: jgstern_agent  # c0d5
  clock: 4  # c0d5
  nonce: c0d5  # c0d5
  message: "PARTIAL FIX MERGED as PR #251 (dev f70cf62fa2). THE ITEM STAYS VIOLATED, and the\nreason is not caution — a named residual is still live and is pinned as a passing\ntest, so the statement does not hold.\n\nWHAT HOLDS NOW, verified by re-running this item's own filed repro rather than by a\nproxy:\n\n  poetry/src/poetry     confirmed -> INCONCLUSIVE at exit 2, naming\n                        cachecontrol, cleo..., dulwich, keyring, requests (51 modules)\n  fastapi-template      confirmed -> INCONCLUSIVE at exit 2, naming\n                        alembic, emails, fastapi... (18 modules)\n  fs_read control       violated / 20 chains, UNCHANGED in both directions\n                        (a violated verdict is not coverage-gated, by design)\n\nMECHANISM: compute_boundary_coverage gained a third blind spot. The permitting case\nis enumerated -- a module supports a clean verdict when the catalog declares a\nprimitive for it or is_stdlib_module knows it. One predicate, both the boundary and\ntaint arms; `catalogs` is a REQUIRED parameter so no caller can silently skip a\nsafety gate.\n\nWHY IT STAYS VIOLATED — the residual, stated rather than papered over. An edge\ncarrying the bare `external` placeholder (an untyped receiver,\npython:external:0-0:get:unresolved) names no module to adjudicate and is NOT counted.\nSo a repo whose I/O is reached ONLY through untyped receivers still gets `confirmed`\ntoday. That was a deliberate scope call: the placeholder population is the largest\nedge population in a Python repo, it identifies no library to report, and counting it\nwould send nearly every repo to inconclusive while telling the reader nothing. It is\nthe receiver-typing gap, INV-linub L3, and closing THIS item requires closing that.\nPinned by test_untyped_receiver_population_is_the_disclosed_residual so a later PR\nthat changes the decision has to argue with an assertion.\n\nTWO THINGS THE FIRST DRAFT GOT WRONG, both caught by measuring on a real repo and\nneither by a test:\n  * it counted `imports` edges -- 231 of the 258 modules it reported on poetry. An\n    import performs no I/O; the catalog classifies CALL SITES.\n  * it blamed poetry's own modules -- 120 of the remaining 171. An unresolved\n    first-party callee is not a catalogue gap, because its source WAS read and\n    whatever I/O it performs was examined on its own edges. supply_chain.tier cannot\n    discriminate these (it reads 3 for every external_symbol node), so first-party is\n    derived from the src side of the edge set.\n\nSTILL NOT MEASURED: any non-Python language; the false-downgrade direction beyond the\nfixtures and these two repos (does the gate ever downgrade a verdict that was\ngenuinely earned?); whether the taint arm's behaviour changes on any repo other than\nhypergumbo itself (its 18 self-claims are unchanged: 16 inconclusive, 2 violated)."  # c0d5
